: "facebook.com/goarmy", "linkedin_url": "linkedin.com/company/us-army"}, "summary": "Brigade Signal Officer /S6 for the 4th Infantry Brigade Combat Team (IBCT), 1st Infantry Division consisting of two Infantry Battalions, a Cavalry Squadron, a Field Artillery Battalion, a Brigade Support Battalion, and a Brigade Special Troops Battalion; serves as the prinicple advisor to the Commander for the employment of communications equipment to include: two Joint Network Nodes (JNN), sixteen Command Post Nodes (CPN), seventeen Sattelite Transmission Trailers (STT), the Army Battle Command System (ABCS), the Command Post of the Future (CPOF), eight enterprise servers, more than two thousand laptop computers, and hundreds of Combat Net Radio (CNR) Systems. Responsible for supervising 3 officers, ninteen non-commissioned officers, and seven junior enlisted officers. Performed duties while simultaneously fulfilling the role of Brigade Automations Management Officer during Combat Operations.", "end_date": "2010-09", "is_primary": false, "start_date": "2010-04", "location_names": []}, {"title": {"name": "assistant battalion intelligence officer", "role": null, "levels": [], "sub_role": null}, "company": {"id": "us-army", "name": "us army", "size": "10001+", "founded": "1775", "website": "goarmy.com", "industry": "military", "location": {"geo": "38.89,-77.08", "name": "arlington, virginia, united states", "metro": "district of columbia", "region": "virginia", "country": "united states", "locality": "arlington", "continent": "north america", "postal_code": null, "address_line_2": null, "street_address": "1500 army navy drive"}, "linkedin_id": "1223", "twitter_url": "twitter.com/goarmy", "facebook_url": "facebook.com/goarmy", "linkedin_url": "linkedin.com/company/us-army"}, "summary": "Tactical Intelligence Officer for a Stryker Infantry Battalion deployed in support of Operation Iraqi Freedom. Assists the Battalion Intelligence Officer in providing timely and accurate intelligence analysis for the Battalion Commander, Company Commanders and staff sections with a focus on Military Operations in Urbanized Terrain (MOUT), limited visibility and precision operations. Acts as the Battalion Intelligence officer in his absence and oversees daily operations of the S-2 Section. Manages battalion information, and the Physical and Personnel Security Program. Integrates Digital Systems in intelligence collection and dissemination. Develops and supervises a 4-man section and performs direct liaison with the Battalion Reconnaissance Platoon and Sniper Section to manage intelligence collection assets. Conducts battle tracking and supervises TOC intelligence operations during training and contingency operations.", "end_date": "2007-11", "is_primary": false, "start_date": "2006-11", "location_names": []}, {"title": {"name": "anti-armor platoon leader", "role": null, "levels": ["manager"], "sub_role": null}, "company": {"id": "us-army", "name": "us army", "size": "10001+", "founded": "1775", "website": "goarmy.com", "industry": "military", "location": {"geo": "38.89,-77.08", "name": "arlington, virginia, united states", "metro": "district of columbia", "region": "virginia", "country": "united states", "locality": "arlington", "continent": "north america", "postal_code": null, "address_line_2": null, "street_address": "1500 army navy drive"}, "linkedin_id": "1223", "twitter_url": "twitter.com/goarmy", "facebook_url": "facebook.com/goarmy", "linkedin_url": "linkedin.com/company/us-army"}, "summary": "Stryker Anti-Tank Platoon Leader in a forward deployed Stryker Brigade Combat team, consisting of three Anti-Tank Guided Missile Stryker Vehicles. Responsible for the health, welfare, Morale, training and professional development of five Non-commissioned Officers, and six Soldiers. Responsible for the combat readiness, maintenance, and accountability of more than 7 million dollars worth of equipment. Conducts combat support operations; defeats all armor threats and e